summary:
A US education nonprofit headquartered in Washington, DC, authorised by Congress in 2008 and launched in 2011. Its AI work includes:
- an AI literacy framework (2024) built on understanding, evaluating and using AI, with 'human judgment' and 'centering justice' as core values;
- the Responsibly Designed AI certification for edtech products (launched April 2025);
- research such as the U-GAIN Reading R&D centre on generative AI in reading instruction;
- professional learning for school districts.
In April 2026 it began a three-year partnership with TNTP, funded by Salesforce, to help schools integrate AI.
